## Add public Simulation API and sandbox graph source on queries
================================================================================

Context: Operators could create and run what-if scenarios in the UI, and
Explorer already picked a ready sandbox, but the external REST catalog,
SPARQL playground, Knowledge Graph reads, and MCP tools still hit only
the live graph. Programmatic callers needed CRUD + run, and every graph
query surface needed the same sandbox overlay as Explorer.

Changes:

1. src/api/routers/simulation.py
   External CRUD, run, abort, purge, diff, runs, and task poll at
   /api/v1/simulations.
2. src/api/external_app.py
   Mount the Simulation router with the Simulation OpenAPI tag.
3. src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py
   triples / triples/find / stats accept simulation_id and
   include_inferred (same overlay as Explorer).
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/query/TwinSandboxSparql.py
   Read-only SPARQL against a ready sandbox snapshot (RDFLib, 20k cap).
5. src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   POST /dtwin/execute routes sandbox SPARQL when simulation_id is set.
6. src/mcp-server/server/simulation_tools.py
   MCP list_simulations, select_simulation, create_simulation,
   run_simulation.
7. src/mcp-server/server/session.py
   domain_params and GraphQL body inject the selected sandbox.
8. src/front/static/query/js/query-api.js
   Settings → API Graph picker appends simulation_id on graph queries.
9. docs/api.md
   Document the Simulation API and simulation_id on KG reads.

